1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,544
GhostWatch: a séance for software. Coding agents are black boxes that can do real

2
00:00:06,544 --> 00:00:12,765
damage and die when they crash. So we summon an AI ghost into a real Freestyle VM,

3
00:00:12,765 --> 00:00:18,227
stream it live to everyone, and keep its state in a Terse durable actor.

4
00:00:18,833 --> 00:00:24,433
Browsers connect to one durable Ghost actor. A disposable worker runs the OpenAI

5
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:29,824
agent, executes tools in the VM, and writes every step back, with an Exorcist

6
00:00:29,824 --> 00:00:31,294
screening everything.

7
00:00:32,024 --> 00:00:37,533
Here's the live séance: two browsers, both connected to the same Terse durable

8
00:00:37,533 --> 00:00:37,956
actor.

9
00:00:39,722 --> 00:00:42,276
I make a wish, and summon the ghost.

10
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:51,832
A fresh Freestyle VM boots in under a second. The OpenAI ghost narrates and runs

11
00:00:51,832 --> 00:00:54,454
real commands, streamed live.

12
00:00:57,679 --> 00:01:01,571
It writes the whole app into the VM.

13
00:01:03,178 --> 00:01:07,804
Another spectator throws a curse: make it rain bats.

14
00:01:08,924 --> 00:01:14,988
A malicious rm -rf curse? The Exorcist blocks it instantly.

15
00:01:16,132 --> 00:01:19,461
Now I kill -9 the worker, mid-build.

16
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:28,180
It restarts and re-enters the same VM. Nothing lost: the state lives in the actor.

17
00:01:29,425 --> 00:01:33,561
The ghost publishes its app on a public URL.

18
00:01:38,567 --> 00:01:44,235
And here's the real app, bats included, served from the Freestyle VM.

19
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:51,198
GhostWatch. Code on GitHub. Happy Halloween!
